<Base title="English" description="Young Turing Program (YTP): a Taiwan-based youth software talent program by SYSTEX — algorithm competition, mentored projects, hackathon and overseas study visits.">
  <div class="wrap page-head">
    <h1>Young Turing Program</h1>
    <p class="lead measure">It is now the era that software defines everything. Encourage young talents to dream, and make the world a better place through their logical thinking and innovative abilities.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <h2>About</h2>
    <p>The Young Turing Program (YTP), named after Alan Turing, the father of computer science, is a social good initiative of SYSTEX Corporation, running in Taiwan since 2016. Junior-high and senior-high students form teams of three, take an online preliminary round, then a one-day on-site algorithm contest in Taipei. Top senior-high teams go on to a mentored project stage with university professors and industry volunteers, a hackathon, and a selection for an overseas study visit to Silicon Valley companies and university labs.</p>
    <h2>Season {season.year}</h2>
    <Track />
    <h2>International program (iYTP)</h2>
    <p>YTP has previously run an international edition for senior-high students in the Asia-Pacific region (registration on the old site last updated for the 2023 season, with a coding competition in September and a project challenge and free visit to Taiwan the following year).</p>
